      "writtenOn": "2020-05-30T20:20:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This happens when PE goes into PE_WAIT_FOR_ERROR_RECOVERY.  It will call tc_start_error_recovery for the TC to handle recovery from the TypeC point of view.  I was seeing this with a hard reset, which is why I called that out.\n\nTCPCI raises a fault-0x01 (I2C) when something that is not valid occurs when an I2C write happens over the TCPCI. This is not an indication that the I2C interface had a problem. In most of these situations that I have seen there is some tie in to AutoDischargeDisconnect being enabled or disabled when it should not be.",
